<div class="page-frame">
  <div id="title"<%=' class=post' if Time.now > Time.new(2015, 7, 6, 11, 00, 00, "-07:00") %>></div>
  <div id="back"><a href="/">Back to <em>TERA</em></a></div>

  <div id="t-content">
    <div class="intro">
      <h1>Wild New Update for <em>TERA</em></h1>
      <div class="video">
        <div class="overlay" data-embed="JkM3HxRJ4U8"></div>
      </div>
      <p>On July 7, all of <em>TERA</em> can Go Berserk! We're adding goodies like <strong>new berserker skills</strong> for tanking, a <strong>dressing room</strong> for costume previews, three sets of <strong>tier 7 gear</strong>, and lots more content! Enjoy the return of Shattered Fleet, the all-new <strong>Timescape dungeon</strong>, and a revamped <strong>Kaprima</strong>. Plus an all-new raid dungeon—<strong>Akeron's Inferno</strong>—and the big <strong>Gridiron battleground</strong>.</p>
    </div>

    <div id="skills" class="skills">
      <h1>Go Berserk for New Skills</h1>
      <p>Berserkers, we know you’d kill for the ability to tank. Well, take a deep breath, check out your new tanking skills available at level 65, and start intimidating enemies.</p>
      <p><span class="icon intimidation"></span><strong>Intimidation</strong> is the key to berserker tanking. While      active, this skill generates aggro around the berserker, increases attack aggro, and reduces crits. Intimidation also alters Axe Block, Flatten, Staggering Strike, Fiery Rage, Raze, and Unchained Anger, adding new effects that increase aggro, decrease damage, and restore HP.</p>
      <p>Four other new skills give Berserkers all they need to tank:</p>
      <ul>
        <li class="block">
          <h4><span class="icon evasive"></span>Evasive Roll</h4>
          <p>Dodge enemy attacks while Intimidation is active.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="block">
          <h4><span class="icon counter"></span>Axe Counter</h4>
          <p>A counterattack usable while Intimidation is active that increases knockdown resistance and reduces damage taken while attacking.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="block">
          <h4><span class="icon overwhelm"></span>Overwhelm</h4>
          <p>Rush a distant enemy and attack, often knocking down that monster.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="block">
          <h4><span class="icon punishing"></span>Punishing Strike</h4>
          <p>A quick attack usable while Intimidation is active that generates high aggro. Follow up with a second Punishing Strike to decrease the target’s Endurance.</p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div id="timescape" class="timescape unlocked">
      <h1>Run Amuck in Timescape</h1>
      <p>Time and space are being fractured deep down inside the Time Core. Battle your way through dragons, kumas, and floating islands of rock to face Yana before the master of time and space can shatter the bubble of the dream. This 5-player dungeon for level 65 characters offers both normal and hard modes. Parties will face:</p>
      <ul class="disc">
        <li><strong>Hemera, the white dragon;</strong></li>
        <li><strong>Eremes, the black dragon (in hard mode);</strong></li>
        <li><strong>Tempas, the Kumas of Storms; and</strong></li>
        <li><strong>Yana, the many-faced master of time and space.</strong></li>
      </ul>
      <ul class="screens">
        <li>
          <a href="http://tera-cdn0.enmasse-game.com/datastore/images/2015/06/24/20/43/31/632/Timescape_06.jpg" class="screen left"></a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="http://tera-cdn0.enmasse-game.com/datastore/images/2015/06/24/20/43/31/696/Timescape_04.jpg" class="screen middle"></a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="http://tera-cdn0.enmasse-game.com/datastore/images/2015/06/24/20/43/31/138/Timescape_03.jpg" class="screen right"></a>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div id="akeron" class="akeron unlocked">
      <h1>Get Fired Up in Akeron’s Inferno</h1>
      <p>Imprisoned gods are always best left imprisoned, especially when that god is the ultra-violent alter ego of the Father of Dragons — Saleron. Enter Akeron’s Inferno from Wyrmgorge, prevent the destruction of the Godbinder, and stop Akeron from escaping his prison. This new 10-player raid dungeon for level 65 players offers both normal and hard modes. Parties will face:</p>
      <ul class="disc">
        <li><strong>Darumag, the nigh-invulnerable fimbrilisk;</strong></li>
        <li><strong>Magnarox, a BAM intent on destroying the Godbinder;</strong></li>
        <li><strong>Sammar-Sal, a fiery hydrath demon; and</strong></li>
        <li><strong>Duras, the stone giant puppet of Akeron.</strong></li>
      </ul>
      <ul class="screens">
        <li>
          <a href="http://tera-cdn0.enmasse-game.com/datastore/images/2015/06/24/20/37/20/506/Akerons_05.jpg" class="screen left"></a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="http://tera-cdn0.enmasse-game.com/datastore/images/2015/06/24/20/37/19/441/Akerons_04.jpg" class="screen middle"></a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="http://tera-cdn0.enmasse-game.com/datastore/images/2015/06/24/20/37/19/27/Akerons_01.jpg" class="screen right"></a>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div id="gridiron" class="gridiron unlocked">
      <h1>Go Savage in Gridiron</h1>
      <p>Two teams enter, everybody dies! A lot! Gridiron drops you into the middle of an enormous, open factory floor with only one rule — kill as many members of the opposing team as you can in 10 minutes. Stand on the grating in the center and fight or seek buffs from the statues along the walkways. Either way, you must kill to win, or die trying.</p>
      <p><strong>Battleground features</strong></p>
      <ul class="disc">
        <li><strong>15 vs 15 PvP battleground</strong></li>
        <li><strong>Team deathmatch structure</strong></li>
        <li><strong>First team to amass 70 kills wins</strong></li>
        <li><strong>Strategically placed statues provide buffs</strong></li>
      </ul>
      <ul class="screens">
        <li>
          <a href="http://tera-cdn0.enmasse-game.com/datastore/images/2015/06/24/20/39/56/319/GridIron_04.jpg" class="screen left"></a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="http://tera-cdn0.enmasse-game.com/datastore/images/2015/06/24/20/39/56/148/GridIron_03.jpg" class="screen middle"></a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="http://tera-cdn0.enmasse-game.com/datastore/images/2015/06/24/20/39/56/359/GridIron_02.jpg" class="screen right"></a>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div id="dressing" class="dressing">
      <h1>Preview Your Wild Side in the Dressing Room</h1>
      <div class="video">
        <div class="overlay" data-embed="Y0eayFNqyh8"></div>
      </div>
      <p>Pull the curtain closed in the Dressing Room and go wild trying on any cosmetic item for your race and class available in the <em>TERA</em> store.</p>
      <ul class="disc">
        <li><strong>Preview costumes, weapon skins, mounts, and pets.</strong></li>
